WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.600
vancouver finished 6,000 8 net new homes, 6% over its yearly target. This is vancouver daily,

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:13.640
episode 66. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. I don't live in vancouver. After that housing

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:18.160
count, a regulation rollback from the premiere, then a surrey mayor who wants the regional

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:23.200
chair's job in order to end the way that job works. The city of vancouver's own staff report,

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:29.920
written up by Daily Hive, covers the year from October 1st, 2025 through September 30th, 2026.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:35.600
The legislative target under the Housing Supply Act was 5,684 homes.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:39.020
Completions ran about 24% ahead of the year before that.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:46.080
Staff got to the net figure by counting 6,809 finished units and taking off 801 demolitions.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:54.380
Since October 2023, the city is at 14,989 net new homes, about 92% of a three-year target

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:59.760
of 16,281, still 1,292 short of that milestone.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:05.800
Staff say projects already in the pipeline can still reach the 5-year requirement of 28,900

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:07.300
by September 2028.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:15.120
Rental made up 4,653 of this year's net homes, about 77% against provincial guidance of 72.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:22.300
two. Of those rental homes, 824 met the income-based affordability benchmark, about 18% where the

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:27.980
guidance called for 38. Premier Lauren Dorkson has indicated his government will abolish the Bill 43

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:33.860
municipal targets. A change in the law is not expected until the legislature sits in spring 2027,

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:38.340
and staff say this filing could be Vancouver's last report under the act as it stands.

00:01:39.455 --> 00:01:43.555
Premier Lauren Dorkson wants two old rules gone for every new one the province writes.

00:01:43.555 --> 00:01:48.095
Daily high reports he has put Carson Binda, Minister of State for Red Tape

00:01:48.095 --> 00:01:52.975
Production and the MLA for Vancouver, Colchena in charge of that work. A mandate

00:01:52.975 --> 00:01:58.035
letter dated November 24th, 2026, tells Binda to work with other ministers so

00:01:58.035 --> 00:02:02.695
regulatory requirements are back at 2017 levels by the end of this term. The

00:02:02.695 --> 00:02:06.895
letter's own line is, introduce and implement a one-in, two-out rule for

00:02:06.895 --> 00:02:11.475
regulatory reform throughout government. Environment Minister Alia Warbus is told

00:02:11.475 --> 00:02:16.275
to bring legislation that repeals clean B.C. and the regulations tied to it, and zero

00:02:16.275 --> 00:02:20.615
emission vehicle sales quotas and puts firm deadlines on each stage of environmental

00:02:20.615 --> 00:02:21.315
assessments.

00:02:21.995 --> 00:02:26.535
Housing ministers Kathy Aunstedt and Zishon Walla are told to speed development approvals,

00:02:26.955 --> 00:02:32.195
review the B.C. building code to cut construction costs, overhaul the step code, and give municipalities

00:02:32.195 --> 00:02:34.535
control of residential development again.

00:02:35.175 --> 00:02:39.395
Surrey Mayor Doug McCallum is running for Metro Vancouver Chair, C.B.C. reports.

00:02:39.395 --> 00:02:43.035
A day after Burnaby Mayor Mike Hurley said he would leave that seat.

00:02:43.575 --> 00:02:47.555
McCallum says that if he wins, he will work with the B.C. conservatives to remake the

00:02:47.555 --> 00:02:51.135
regional body into something unlike any other regional government in the province.

00:02:51.675 --> 00:02:54.635
One where local governments have no direct say over utilities.

00:02:55.752 --> 00:03:01.532
Stephen Brown has been ordered to pay Rakesh Duna $4,262,369.

00:03:02.992 --> 00:03:07.892
The Vancouver Sun reports the B.C. Court of Appeal let a default judgment stand after Brown

00:03:07.892 --> 00:03:12.812
signed a 2021 deal to buy a West Vancouver house for $18 million and never closed.

00:03:13.332 --> 00:03:17.212
When Dunner re-listed, the best price he could get was just under $14 million.

00:03:17.792 --> 00:03:22.312
Brown missed the 21-day deadline to respond, and a default judgment followed less than two

00:03:22.312 --> 00:03:28.212
months after the suit was filed. A 2023 hearing he did not attend set the damages. In 2025,

00:03:28.392 --> 00:03:32.352
he tried to have the judgment set aside. This week, Justice Jeffrey Gomory,

00:03:32.592 --> 00:03:37.372
for a unanimous three-judge panel, said Brown's failure to respond was willful and deliberate,

00:03:37.372 --> 00:03:39.372
it and not at all inadvertent.

00:03:39.512 --> 00:03:44.392
Gomerie noted Brown is a CEO who called himself a sophisticated businessman, had dealt with

00:03:44.392 --> 00:03:48.612
lawsuits in Canada and the United States, and had hired a lawyer in a separate proceeding

00:03:48.612 --> 00:03:49.532
in 2021.

