00:05:03.402 --> 00:05:09.062
A lawsuit filed November 25 in BC Supreme Court in New Westminster alleges Ian Hunt killed

00:05:09.062 --> 00:05:12.282
his wife, Trina Hunt, and should not profit from her death.

00:05:12.782 --> 00:05:16.582
Global news says the plaintiffs are her mother, her brother, and her sister-in-law.

00:05:16.962 --> 00:05:22.862
The claim alleges that on or about January 14 through 15, 2021, at or near Port Moody,

00:05:22.862 --> 00:05:30.022
Hunt intentionally caused her death by means the family says are unknown to them, but known to him in circumstances amounting to murder.

00:05:30.562 --> 00:05:33.862
No one has been charged with murder and the cause of death is still unknown.

00:05:34.462 --> 00:05:39.622
On February 4, 2025, Hunt was charged with one count of indignity to human remains.

00:05:40.142 --> 00:05:49.082
Police in court documents alleged he disposed of her body in the woods at or near Port Moody and Hope, January 16, 2021, two days before he reported her missing.

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:51.842
He has made dozens of appearances on that charge.

00:05:52.162 --> 00:05:55.342
The trial has been pushed back repeatedly, and he is out of custody.

00:05:55.882 --> 00:05:58.922
The criminal trial is not set until October 20, 2077.

00:05:59.422 --> 00:06:03.642
The civil claim says he inherited her estate and assets through her will or other law.

00:06:04.122 --> 00:06:08.582
Argus, he should not benefit from an illegal or dishonourable act and asks that the assets

00:06:08.582 --> 00:06:10.682
go to her mother, Diana May Ibit.

00:06:11.222 --> 00:06:12.662
None of this has been proven in court.

00:06:13.162 --> 00:06:15.762
Global news contacted his lawyers and got no response.

00:06:16.222 --> 00:06:17.782
He has 30 days to file one.

00:06:17.782 --> 00:06:25.542
The filing says the couple's port moody home was bought in 2006 for $632,230 and allegedly

00:06:25.542 --> 00:06:29.022
sold in May 2023 for $1.925 million.

00:06:29.462 --> 00:06:32.082
Her mother is claiming half of that property or the proceeds.

00:06:32.622 --> 00:06:36.742
The claim says he then bought a house in Harrison Mills with money from that sale, and

00:06:36.742 --> 00:06:41.162
Ibit wants half of that property or its proceeds, plus a certificate of pending litigation

00:06:41.162 --> 00:06:41.862
against it.

00:06:42.242 --> 00:06:46.642
The family also wants an accounting of other assets and an order stopping him from disposing

00:06:46.642 --> 00:06:48.102
of assets while the case is on.

00:06:48.622 --> 00:06:52.542
They alleged he misled them and police by saying he knew nothing about her disappearance,

00:06:52.982 --> 00:06:57.382
and by reporting her missing when, they alleged he knew she was already dead and knew where

00:06:57.382 --> 00:06:58.022
her body was.

00:06:58.522 --> 00:07:02.702
They alleged he first took part in a reward for information that they believed him and

00:07:02.702 --> 00:07:06.622
searched harder because they thought she might be alive, and that this caused continuing

00:07:06.622 --> 00:07:09.922
mental anguish amounting to intentional inflection of mental suffering.

00:07:10.362 --> 00:07:14.842
They wanted declaration that he killed her, a bar on inheriting, the assets returned,

00:07:14.842 --> 00:07:19.702
and punitive exemplary and aggravated damages, plus damages for that suffering.

